=== Threads ===
It's like an worker which is working in a process
+ Process may have some workers

== Native Threads ==
"Virtual threads"

= Daemon x User =
User: JVM closes the program when all Daemon Threads was closed
Daemon: Lower priority, are responsible for Garbage Collector

== Thread States ==
New -> Runnable <--> Running ->
Waiting/Blocked
Waiting Blocked -> Runnable
Running -> Dead

= Meanings =
Runnable = ready to run
Running = running (doing what he was desired to do)
Waiting/Blocked = waiting for the next command / blocked by a command (sleeping)
Dead = dead thread (impossible to do anything)
